# Claude Code project-local files
.claude/

# The instance's configuration. DEPLOYMENT-SCOPED, never committed: install.sh
# writes it from config.template.yaml (the committed defaults) when absent, and
# an operator edits it per machine. Services Standard § Centralized config.yaml.
config.yaml

# Legacy service config (replaced by config.yaml — kept for backwards compat)
scripts/services/*.config.env

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Test run output — ephemeral, per Testing Standard § What Does NOT Go in tests/
testing/logs/

# PLATFORM-WRITTEN, NOT OURS, AND IT WAS NEVER REPRODUCIBLE FROM HERE.
# `~/.claude/skills/` symlinks to `config/skills/`, so the Claude platform's
# skill-sync writes INTO version control on every sync round, on every machine,
# forever. That is a second agent writing the declaration — crosswise to the
# declarative-convergence position, where `config/` is the declaration and
# `install.sh` is the only agent that realises it.
#
# UNTRACKED 2026-10-03 after SN-PM2 measured the mechanism. 447 files, and the
# whole git history for the path is TWO commits — both mine, both from the same
# day, both accidental `git add -A config/` sweeps of platform churn. Nothing
# here was ever authored by this repo.
#
# Reproducibility is not lost because it never existed: a rebuilt box gets these
# skills from the platform, not from the clone. It is the category CLAUDE.md
# already carves out as machine-local, beside `projects/`, `sessions/` and
# `cache/`. Tracking it only generated cross-machine conflicts — it had already
# latently blocked SN-PM2's checkout from fast-forwarding.
config/skills/synced/
